===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|genom}}, from {{der|en|de|Genom}}, {{coin|de|Hans Winkler|nat=German|occ=botanist|in=1920|nocap=1|nocat=1}} as a {{blend|de|Gen|Chromosom||t1=gene|t2=chromosome|nocap=1|nocat=1}}.<ref>{{cite-book|last=Winkler|first=Hans|authorlink=Hans Winkler|title=Verbreitung und Ursache der Parthenogenesis im Pflanzen- und Tierreiche|url=https://archive.org/details/verbreitungundur00wink/page/165/mode/2up?q=Genom|page=165|year=1920|publisher=Verlag Fischer|location=Jena}}</ref><ref name="ODO">{{R:Lexico}}</ref><ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref> {{surf|+suf|en|gene|ome|alt1=gen(e)}}, or a {{blend|en|gene|chromosome|alt1=gen(e)|alt2=(chromos)ome||nocap=1}}. Spelling altered to reflect the surface analysis.

